WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.199
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEIC preparation.

2
00:00:05.499 --> 00:00:08.804
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.104 --> 00:00:18.467
Unit three: Part 1: Photographs of Objects and Places. Today you will describe objects, positions and scenes using passive and place language.

4
00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:21.420
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:25.704
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:27.319
Shelf.

7
00:00:28.317 --> 00:00:31.117
Shelf means a flat board for putting things on.

8
00:00:31.717 --> 00:00:33.008
Books are on the shelf.

9
00:00:33.617 --> 00:00:36.466
Your turn. Say: Shelf.

10
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.185
Shelf.

11
00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:41.858
Be stacked.

12
00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:45.720
Be stacked means to be piled one on top of another.

13
00:00:46.317 --> 00:00:48.189
Boxes are stacked by the wall.

14
00:00:48.783 --> 00:00:51.494
Your turn. Say: Be stacked.

15
00:00:54.333 --> 00:00:55.242
Be stacked.

16
00:00:55.983 --> 00:00:57.159
Be displayed.

17
00:00:58.150 --> 00:01:00.869
Be displayed means to be shown for people to see.

18
00:01:01.483 --> 00:01:02.995
Products are displayed.

19
00:01:03.583 --> 00:01:06.050
Your turn. Say: Be displayed.

20
00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:10.064
Be displayed.

21
00:01:10.817 --> 00:01:11.702
Be parked.

22
00:01:12.717 --> 00:01:15.517
Be parked means to be left in a place (vehicles).

23
00:01:16.117 --> 00:01:17.826
Cars are parked outside.

24
00:01:18.417 --> 00:01:20.756
Your turn. Say: Be parked.

25
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:24.555
Be parked.

26
00:01:25.317 --> 00:01:26.422
Beside.

27
00:01:27.417 --> 00:01:29.045
Beside means next to.

28
00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:31.452
A lamp is beside the desk.

29
00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:34.226
Your turn. Say: Beside.

30
00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:38.033
Beside.

31
00:01:38.783 --> 00:01:39.610
Above.

32
00:01:40.617 --> 00:01:42.291
Above means higher than.

33
00:01:42.883 --> 00:01:44.593
A clock is above the door.

34
00:01:45.183 --> 00:01:47.940
Your turn. Say: Above.

35
00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:51.755
Above.

36
00:01:52.517 --> 00:01:53.402
Empty.

37
00:01:54.417 --> 00:01:56.521
Empty means with nothing inside.

38
00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.373
The room is empty.

39
00:01:58.983 --> 00:02:01.032
Your turn. Say: Empty.

40
00:02:03.867 --> 00:02:04.810
Empty.

41
00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:06.423
Pavement.

42
00:02:07.417 --> 00:02:09.776
Pavement means the path beside a road.

43
00:02:10.383 --> 00:02:12.151
People walk on the pavement.

44
00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:15.159
Your turn. Say: Pavement.

45
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:18.885
Pavement.

46
00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:23.664
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.517 --> 00:02:27.143
Visal, what if the photograph has no people?

48
00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:41.395
Then the correct statement usually describes objects and their position, often with the passive: boxes are stacked against the wall, or chairs have been arranged in rows.

49
00:02:42.483 --> 00:02:44.030
What language should I know?

50
00:02:45.117 --> 00:02:55.696
Learn prepositions such as beside, above, behind and along, and passive forms like is displayed, is parked and is being repaired.

51
00:02:56.783 --> 00:02:58.075
How can I get ready?

52
00:02:59.183 --> 00:03:07.861
Look at every object and decide where it is. Predict the sentence before the audio, and then compare it with what you hear.

53
00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.558
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.417 --> 00:03:16.052
Grammar focus: Strategy: objects, positions, passive forms.

55
00:03:16.352 --> 00:03:17.550
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:20.203
Boxes are stacked beside the door.

57
00:03:21.117 --> 00:03:23.105
Products are displayed on the shelves.

58
00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:30.782
When there are no people, focus on objects, positions and passive forms. Predict a sentence before you listen.

59
00:03:31.517 --> 00:03:35.272
Be careful! Don't say: I describe feelings in the photograph.

60
00:03:37.233 --> 00:03:40.150
Say: I describe objects and positions.

61
00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:42.090
Objects and places.

62
00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.413
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.549
An Empty Shop.

64
00:03:47.849 --> 00:03:50.464
The photograph shows a small shop in the morning.

65
00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:53.455
Products are displayed on the shelves.

66
00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.687
Some boxes are stacked beside the door.

67
00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:00.524
A bicycle is parked on the pavement outside.

68
00:04:01.533 --> 00:04:03.858
No customers are visible yet.

69
00:04:04.967 --> 00:04:09.166
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:10.017 --> 00:04:12.933
When there are no people, statements describe blank.

71
00:04:13.233 --> 00:04:18.268
A, objects and positions. B, feelings. C, future plans.

72
00:04:21.833 --> 00:04:24.413
The answer is A: objects and positions.

73
00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:27.480
Boxes are blank beside the door.

74
00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:31.538
A, stacking. B, stacked. C, stack.

75
00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:36.798
The answer is B: stacked.

76
00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:39.415
Where is the bicycle?

77
00:04:39.715 --> 00:04:44.135
A, inside the shop. B, on the shelf. C, on the pavement.

78
00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:49.665
The answer is C: on the pavement.

79
00:04:50.817 --> 00:04:52.781
Which preposition means 'higher than'?

80
00:04:53.081 --> 00:04:56.398
A, above. B, beside. C, behind.

81
00:04:59.933 --> 00:05:01.619
The answer is A: above.

82
00:05:02.783 --> 00:05:04.632
What is displayed on the shelves?

83
00:05:04.932 --> 00:05:08.713
A, cars. B, products. C, people.

84
00:05:12.267 --> 00:05:14.406
The answer is B: products.

85
00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.868
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:19.717 --> 00:05:22.215
How do you describe a photograph with no people?

87
00:05:31.017 --> 00:05:32.494
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:32.794 --> 00:05:45.097
I look at the objects and decide where each one is. I think of passive forms, such as products are displayed or boxes are stacked. I also use prepositions of place like beside and above.

89
00:05:45.397 --> 00:05:47.141
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:54.058
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: objects, positions, passive forms.

91
00:05:54.358 --> 00:05:58.066
Today's value is attention. Look carefully and listen well.

92
00:05:58.366 --> 00:06:00.694
See you in Unit four. Goodbye!

93
00:06:00.994 --> 00:06:04.586
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

